# [MODULE DOC]
# Tempita template generating _ball_tree.pyx. It instantiates, for float64
# (suffix 64) and float32 (suffix 32) inputs, the BallTree specialization of
# the generic BinaryTree defined in _binary_tree.pxi (included textually).
# Each node is a hypersphere: node_bounds[0, i_node] stores the (optionally
# sample-weighted) centroid and node_data[i_node].radius the maximum distance
# from the centroid to any point of the node. The module-level functions
# allocate_data, init_node, min/max(r)dist and their dual-tree variants are
# the hooks that _binary_tree.pxi calls by name; they make BallTree work for
# any true metric in VALID_METRICS. The public BallTree is the float64 class.
{{py:

